{"file":"Qt Development Skills-1.6.1-v2.zip","bytes":435344,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"qt-development-skills","description":"Agentic engineering skills for Qt software development, including Qt C++/QML code review, QML coding, and Qt C++/QML code documentation. Bundles the hosted Qt Documentation MCP server for live Qt API lookups. These skills use AI and can make mistakes. Always double-check the output carefully.","version":"1.6.1"}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/qt-cmake-project/SKILL.md","name":"qt-cmake-project","description":"Use to generate or update Qt 6 CMake projects or edit CMakeLists.txt, add sources/resources or define targets (executable, QML module, library).","headings":["Overview","Guardrails","When this skill applies","Workflow","Detailed Instructions to Use","Hard rules (apply to every output)","Documentation lookup","Output style","Common-mistakes pre-flight"],"name_hint":"qt · cmake · 项目"},{"path":"skills/qt-cpp-docs/SKILL.md","name":"qt-cpp-docs","description":"Generates standalone Markdown reference documentation for any Qt/C++ source files — Qt Widgets classes, Qt Quick backends, Qt/C++ modules, plain C++ utilities, structs, free-function headers, and entry points like main.cpp. Use this skill to document any .h or .cpp file: Qt classes, plain C++ code, utility helpers, or application startup files. Triggers on: \"document this class\", \"write docs for my C++\", \"document main.cpp\", \"C++ API docs\", \"document my Qt app\", or whenever C++ or header files are provided and documentation is needed. Works with single files, pasted code, or entire project folders. DO NOT use if the user asks for QDoc format output.","headings":["Qt C++ Documentation Skill","Guardrails","Core requirements","Document structure","1. Class Overview","2. Project Structure and Dependencies","3. Class Hierarchy and Role","4. Q_PROPERTY Declarations *(if applicable)*","5. Enumerations (Q_ENUM / Q_FLAG) *(if applicable)*","6. Public Member Variables *(if applicable)*","7. Signals *(if applicable)*","8. Public Slots and Q_INVOKABLE Methods *(if applicable)*","9. Public Methods","10. Protected Virtual Methods / Event Handlers","11. Ownership and Lifecycle","12. Thread Safety","13. QML Exposure *(if applicable)*","14. Inter-Class Interactions"],"name_hint":"qt · cpp · 文档"},{"path":"skills/qt-cpp-review/SKILL.md","name":"qt-cpp-review","description":"Invoke when the user asks to review, check, audit, or look over Qt6 C++ code — or suggest before committing. Runs deterministic linting (60+ rules) then six parallel deep- analysis agents covering model contracts, ownership, threading, API correctness, error handling, and performance. Reports only high-confidence issues (>80/100) with structured mitigations. Read-only — never modifies code.","headings":["Qt Code Review","When to use this skill","Arguments","Framework mode detection","Scope detection","Diff/commit scope (narrow)","Codebase scope (wide)","Execution order","Phase 1: Deterministic linting (scripts)","If python3 is not found, fall back to:","Phase 2: Agent-driven deep analysis (6 parallel agents)","Phase 3: Consolidation and reporting","Agent missions","Agent 1: Model Contracts","Agent 2: Ownership & Lifecycle","Agent 3: Thread Safety","Agent 4: API, Naming & C++ Correctness","Agent 5: Error Handling & Validation"],"name_hint":"qt · cpp · 评审"},{"path":"skills/qt-figma-component-generation/SKILL.md","name":"qt-figma-component-generation","description":"Extract component metadata from a Figma design system and generate production-ready QML controls. Use this skill whenever someone wants to turn Figma components into QML files — whether they say \"generate components from Figma\", \"create QML controls based on a design system\", \"convert Figma components to QML\", \"build the component library\", \"extract button/input/checkbox from Figma\", or anything similar. Requires design-tokens.json and QML design system singletons to already exist (from the token extraction skill). Uses Figma MCP to inspect components one at a time and maps variants, states, sizing, and token usage to idiomatic Qt Quick Controls 2 patterns. Trigger this skill at the component generation step of any QML design-system workflow.","headings":["Figma Component Generation Skill","Prerequisites","Step 1 — Component Discovery","Step 2 — Pattern Selection","Step 3 — Prepare the Chosen Pattern","Pattern A assets — `references/`","Pattern B assets — `assets/qt-controls/`","Step 4 — Per-Component Extraction","What to extract per component","Step 5 — Figma → QML Mapping","Base type selection","Variant → property pattern (Pattern A)","Variant → enum pattern (Pattern B)","State → conditional expression pattern","Icon slot pattern","Sizing — tokens first, literals as fallback","Focus ring pattern","Color animation pattern"],"name_hint":"qt · figma · 组件 · generation"},{"path":"skills/qt-figma-token-extraction/SKILL.md","name":"qt-figma-token-extraction","description":"Extract design tokens, text styles, and variables from a Figma design system and produce a design-tokens.json plus ready-to-use QML singletons. Use this skill whenever someone wants to pull their design system out of Figma — whether they say \"export tokens from Figma\", \"get design tokens\", \"set up my design system\", \"read our Figma design system\", \"get Figma variables into QML\", \"pull our color palette from Figma\", \"import design tokens\", \"extract colors/typography/spacing from Figma\", or similar. Trigger this skill at the start of any design-system workflow that involves a Figma source.","headings":["Figma Token Extraction Skill","Skill Structure","Step 0 — Check Qt Project Setup","Step 1 — Routing Questions","Step 2 — Collect All Figma File Links","MCP Method — Extraction via Figma MCP","Step 1a — Verify Figma MCP is connected","Step 1b — Check for modes","Step 1c — Extract variables","Step 1d — Resolve aliases","curl Method — Extraction from the user's local machine","Step 1a — Set up a Figma Personal Access Token","Step 1b — Verify the PAT works before proceeding","Step 1c — Run the variables extraction","Step 1d — Share the result","Extract Styles","MCP method — Text Styles","curl method — Text Styles"],"name_hint":"qt · figma · 变量/Token · extraction"},{"path":"skills/qt-qml-docs/SKILL.md","name":"qt-qml-docs","description":"Generates standalone Markdown reference documentation for QML components and applications. Use this skill whenever you want to document QML files, create API reference docs for a QML component or module, document a Qt Quick application, or produce developer-facing documentation from .qml source code. Triggers on: \"document this QML\", \"write docs for my QML\", \"create reference docs\", \"document QML component\", \"QML API docs\", \"document my Qt Quick component\", \"document my Qt app\", or any time one or more .qml files are provided and documentation is needed. Works with single files, pasted code, or entire project folders. DO NOT use if the user asks for QDoc format output.","headings":["QML Documentation Skill","Core requirements","Document structure","1. Component Overview","2. Project Structure and Dependencies","3. Component Hierarchy and Role","4. Properties","5. Signals","6. Methods","7. Inter-Component Interactions","8. Usage Example *(reusable components only)*","Pre-flight: check for existing documentation","How to check","Input handling","Parsing QML accurately","Tone and style","Output location","Quality check"],"name_hint":"qt · qml · 文档"},{"path":"skills/qt-qml-profiler/SKILL.md","name":"qt-qml-profiler","description":"Use when the user is investigating QML / Qt Quick performance — both vague complaints (\"the UI feels laggy\", \"this is slow\", \"frames are dropping\", \"the app stutters\") and explicit asks to profile, find hotspots, or optimize bindings, signals, or rendering. Runs qmlprofiler on a 2D QML application, parses the .qtd trace, and analyzes hotspots against the source with frame-time, memory, and pixmap-cache summaries. Does NOT cover Qt Quick 3D.","headings":["Qt QML Profiler Skill","Scope","Guardrails","Arguments","Profiling Profiles","Steps","Step 1 — Locate tools","Step 2 — Build with QML debugging (profiling mode only)","Step 3 — Run qmlprofiler (profiling mode only)","Step 4 — Parse the trace","Step 5 — Analyze hotspots","Step 6 — Write report","Step 7 — Console summary","References"],"name_hint":"qt · qml · profiler"},{"path":"skills/qt-qml-review/SKILL.md","name":"qt-qml-review","description":"Invoke when the user asks to review, check, audit, or look over Qt6 QML code -- or suggest before committing. Runs deterministic linting (47+ rules) then six parallel deep- analysis agents covering bindings, layout, loaders, delegates, states, and performance. Optionally invokes system qmllint for type-level checks. Reports only high-confidence issues (>80/100) with structured mitigations. Read-only -- never modifies code.","headings":["Qt QML Code Review","When to use this skill","Scope detection","Diff/commit scope (narrow)","Codebase scope (wide)","Execution order","Phase 1: Deterministic linting (Python script)","If python3 is not found, fall back to:","Phase 1b: System qmllint (optional)","Phase 2: Agent-driven deep analysis (6 parallel agents)","Phase 3: Consolidation and reporting","Agent missions","Agent 1: Bindings & Properties","Agent 2: Layout & Anchoring","Agent 3: Component Loading & Lifecycle","Agent 4: ListView & Delegate Correctness","Agent 5: States, Transitions & Structure","Agent 6: Performance & Code Quality"],"name_hint":"qt · qml · 评审"},{"path":"skills/qt-qml-test-run/SKILL.md","name":"qt-qml-test-run","description":"Builds and runs Qt Quick Test (qmltestrunner / CTest) for a QML project, then writes a Markdown report. Use for \"run qml tests\", \"run qmltestrunner\".","headings":["Qt QML Test Runner Skill","Scope","Guardrails","Arguments","Steps","Step 1 — Locate Qt and qmltestrunner","Step 2 — Discover the test target","Step 3 — Harness mode","Step 4 — Detect existing CMake test wiring","Step 4a — Module-on-executable check","Step 4b — Propose direct `qmltestrunner` first","Step 5 — Wire up if missing","Step 6 — Build","Step 7 — Run tests","Step 8 — Parse JUnit XML","Step 9 — Write Markdown report","Step 10 — Console summary","References"],"name_hint":"qt · qml · 测试 · run"},{"path":"skills/qt-qml-test/SKILL.md","name":"qt-qml-test","description":"Generates Qt Quick Test cases (TestCase, SignalSpy, tryCompare) for QML components. Use for \"write QML tests\", \"qml test\", \"qt quick test\".","headings":["Qt Quick Test Skill","Scope","Guardrails","Output contract","Workflow","Single document","Multiple documents","Project context (opportunistic, bounded)","Resolving the source import","Canonical template","Testing rules","Imports & structure","Single vs nested components","Properties","Signals & SignalSpy","Mouse & key events","Conventions","Per-control specifics"],"name_hint":"qt · qml · 测试"},{"path":"skills/qt-qml/SKILL.md","name":"qt-qml","description":"Applies QML best practices when producing or working with QML source code. Use whenever QML code is the primary subject: writing, reviewing, fixing, refactoring, optimizing, or debugging QML files, components, or bindings. Do NOT trigger for purely conversational QML questions where no code is produced or examined (e.g. \"explain how anchors work\").","headings":["QML Coding Skill","How to apply this skill","Guardrails","Rules","File organization","Imports","Controls","Component loading","Property bindings","Layouts","ListView and delegates","State management","Animations","Images","Accessibility","Singletons","Internationalization","Performance and rendering"],"name_hint":"qt · qml"},{"path":"skills/qt-ui-design/SKILL.md","name":"qt-ui-design","description":"Design or audit UI for Qt/QML, Qt projects, web, or embedded MPU or MCU targets. Use when creating screens, layouts, navigation, or auditing UX.","headin